1) 从告警标签取 node_name 与 disk_path，登录该主机执行:
1) Take node_name and disk_path from the alert labels, log in to the host, and run du -sh <disk_path>/* | sort -rh | head -20 to find the biggest consumers;
2) It is usually workspaces and historical build artifacts; enable Discard old builds in the job configuration to cap retention;
3) To free space immediately, run the Jenkins Workspace Cleanup or manually delete the workspace directories of finished jobs;
4) Longer term push build artifacts to an artifact repository (Nexus/Artifactory) instead of leaving them on the Jenkins local disk.

1) 从告警标签取 node_name，在 Jenkins 的 Manage N:
1) Take node_name from the alert labels and check the offline reason on the Manage Nodes page (Disconnected, Temporarily offline, or low disk space);
2) If it went offline because of disk or temporary-directory space, clean up workspaces and old build artifacts, then click Bring this node back online;
3) If the agent connection dropped, log in to the agent host and confirm the agent process is alive and the network and port to the master are reachable;
4) If the master itself is unreachable, check the Jenkins process, the reverse proxy, and whether the JVM is hung from an OOM.

1) 从告警标签取 node_name，登录主机执行 ps aux --sort:
1) Take node_name from the alert labels, log in to the host, and run ps aux --sort=-rss | head -15 to find the largest memory consumers;
2) Run dmesg -T | grep -i 'killed process' to see whether an OOM has already happened;
3) If a single build is memory-hungry (parallel Maven/Gradle compilation, front-end bundling), cap -Xmx and parallelism in the job;
4) If the node is persistently tight, lower its executor count or add memory.

1) 从告警标签取任务名，打开该构建的 Console Output，从下往上找:
1) Take the job name from the alert labels, open that build's Console Output, and find the first ERROR/FAILURE reading upwards from the bottom;
2) For compilation or test failures, hand the log and the commit list to the owning developers and decide whether the last merge should be reverted;
3) For environment failures (dependency download, agent disconnect, disk full), fix the infrastructure first and then click Rebuild;
4) If the same job keeps failing, disable its automatic trigger so it stops consuming executors and flooding alerts.

1) 打开 Jenkins 首页的 Build Queue，确认是任务确实变多还:
1) Open the Build Queue on the Jenkins home page and decide whether there are genuinely more jobs or a stuck build is holding an executor;
2) For a stuck build, open its Console Output to see where the last line stopped and abort it if necessary (a Thread Dump shows which step is blocked);
3) If job volume really has grown, add agent nodes or raise the executor count per node (each executor needs enough CPU and memory);
4) Longer term give long-running jobs their own label and node pool so they do not take executors from routine builds.
